title Two branches each append a paragraph, and both come back whole
prompt autonomous loop, Patchouli seat -- mantra and tally lane
rota lap 4201, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; the threshold's own test is to pull one part out and see whether others move, and pulling LineId out of the sort is exactly what this lap did
think The card's own PATCHOULI block named two open things in this lane -- the several-line interleave, and %441's erratum never reaching the foundation. The interleave is the crux, so it took the lap.
think Measured first: mantra/src/weave.rye already publishes merge and annotate, so the module head's claim that closing the interleave "widens Diff" was the thing to press. It does not. The gap is that ONE type answered two questions.
think LineId was identity and document order at once. Two sides appending three lines each from a shared counter took positions N, N+1, N+2 apiece, so the site broke the tie three separate times and the document came back alternating.
think The fix is a second type rather than a wider first one. Place -- run, site, position -- with a run number read once before apply's stamping loop and carried on every line of that edit. The site tie is then settled once for the whole run.
think The identity pair stays exactly as it was, because a position counter runs fresh inside one weave and (pos, site) was already unique. That is what let the order be repaired with no line renamed and no call site of LineId touched.
think Proven from the failing side before it was believed: restoring the elder comparison in Place.less_than makes claim 10 panic at assert(changes == 1), exit 134. Restored, the same claim reads GREEN.
obs The control caught a shape %519 did not name. Its tiebreak plant aimed at a line inside LineId.less_than that STILL STOOD after the order moved -- the sed matched, bytes changed, and the phase exited 0 because the function it broke had stopped deciding anything. plant_matched_nothing stayed quiet; only the verdict loop's demand that every break be caught could see it, and it answered break_not_caught.
obs bound_shrunk stopped being innocent in the same lap: claim 10 merges a union of twelve against a shrink of 8. Raised to 16, the next power of two above it, with the reason written into the control header rather than left for the next reader to rediscover.
obs The QA frame fired and closed by measurement. My first head rewrite read C+ 79 at register 57 against the elder head's B+ 85, because it led with what the module cannot do. Rewritten to lead with what is -- claims held word for word -- it reads B+ 88 at register 83, inside Door's 20 percent.
obs No REDS row booked, and that is the honest reading rather than a gap. Nothing in the tree was wrong: the tiebreak plant was correct until this lap moved the law it aimed at, and the same commit repairs it. The instrument worked.
